    debugfs: Add access restriction option
    =

    Since debugfs include sensitive information it need to be treated
    carefully. But it also has many very useful debug functions for userspa=
ce.
    With this option we can have same configuration for system with
    need of debugfs and a way to turn it off. This gives a extra protection
    for exposure on systems where user-space services with system
    access are attacked.
    =

    When enabled it is needed a kernel command line parameter to be activat=
ed.
    =

    It can be on or off, but also internally on but not seen from user-spac=
e.
    This no-fs mode do not register a debugfs as filesystem, but client can
    register their parts in the internal structures. This data can be readed
    with a debugger or saved with a crashkernel. When it is off clients
    get EPERM error when accessing the functions for registering their
    components.
    =

    Signed-off-by: Peter Enderborg <peter.enderborg@sony.com>

